# CODEOWNERS
# Practice: P9 Collaboration (Tier 1, 36 mentions)
#           P11 Code review  (Tier 1, 33 mentions)
#
# Named owners per area make review a structural requirement rather than a
# favour. Combined with branch protection, this is the mechanism that evidences
# both practices.
#
# Team (Projet 3):
#   @edothecreator        Mohamed ELKHANFAF    - owner, pipeline & security
#   @erraguibiabdelilah   Abdelilah ERRAGUIBI  - backend & API
#   @Hanane-ELFADIL       Hanane ELFADIL       - front-end & abuse-case tests
#   @anasIRISI            Anas HALLOUMI        - infrastructure, monitoring, docs
#
# Role assignment is a proposal and can be rearranged; what matters for P9/P11
# is that every path has a named owner other than the author.
#
# Verify this file is actually honoured by GitHub (unknown or non-collaborator
# usernames are silently ignored, producing a control that enforces nothing):
#   gh api repos/edothecreator/vintage-marketplace-devsecops/codeowners/errors

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                           @edothecreator

# ---- Security-critical paths: owner review always required ----------------
# Changes here can silently disable a control, so they are deliberately routed
# to the person accountable for the pipeline.

/.github/                   @edothecreator
/.github/workflows/         @edothecreator
/.gitleaks.toml             @edothecreator
/.pre-commit-config.yaml    @edothecreator
/SECURITY.md                @edothecreator
/.gitignore                 @edothecreator

# Authentication, authorization and cryptography are the highest-risk code in
# the project. Two-person review is the intent here.
/backend/src/auth/          @edothecreator @erraguibiabdelilah
/backend/src/middleware/    @edothecreator @erraguibiabdelilah

# ---- Feature areas --------------------------------------------------------

/backend/                   @erraguibiabdelilah @edothecreator
/frontend/                  @Hanane-ELFADIL
/backend/tests/             @Hanane-ELFADIL @edothecreator

# Infrastructure, containers, monitoring
/docker/                    @anasIRISI
/infra/                     @anasIRISI @edothecreator
/monitoring/                @anasIRISI

# ---- Documentation --------------------------------------------------------
# Deliverables, so still reviewed - but not by the pipeline owner alone.

/docs/                      @anasIRISI @edothecreator
/docs/threat-model/         @edothecreator @anasIRISI
/docs/adr/                  @edothecreator
/evidence/                  @edothecreator
/tasks/                     @edothecreator
